1
00:00:03,618 --> 00:00:06,553
Initial reports suggest a terrorist involvement,

2
00:00:06,654 --> 00:00:11,658
but this morning some intelligence experts
have claimed the incidents may be a stunt.

3
00:00:11,759 --> 00:00:16,530
The first sightings were of UFOs
over the Taj Mahal in India.

4
00:00:16,631 --> 00:00:19,333
They came in just after midnight.

5
00:00:19,434 --> 00:00:24,104
In London this morning,
there were reports of men in historic dress

6
00:00:24,205 --> 00:00:25,672
firing upon police.

7
00:00:25,773 --> 00:00:27,774
POLICEMAN : Down, down, down.

8
00:00:27,876 --> 00:00:30,611
Some religious groups are claiming
events overnight

9
00:00:30,712 --> 00:00:33,313
are a vindication of their teachings.

10
00:00:35,283 --> 00:00:37,417
Do you think it is terrorists?

11
00:00:37,519 --> 00:00:40,621
Terrorists bomb things. This is different.

12
00:00:40,722 --> 00:00:43,290
People didn't believe us. Now they should.

13
00:00:43,391 --> 00:00:47,961
Judgement Day is finally here.
This is the End of Days.

14
00:00:59,641 --> 00:01:02,075
"And I heard but did not understand

15
00:01:02,176 --> 00:01:05,946
"and I said, 'Master, what is the end
of all these things?'

16
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:11,184
"And he said, 'Go, Daniel, for the things are
closed up and sealed until the end of time."'

17
00:01:11,286 --> 00:01:13,921
Daniel 12, verse 10.

18
00:01:14,022 --> 00:01:15,856
GWEN : Sounds a bit close for comfort.

19
00:01:15,957 --> 00:01:19,192
This machine's on the blink. Keeps losing power.

20
00:01:19,928 --> 00:01:23,864
Sorry, don't let me stop your portents of doom.
Or have you finished?

21
00:01:23,965 --> 00:01:26,266
No. Plenty more where that came from.

22
00:01:26,367 --> 00:01:29,703
Abaddon, the Great Devourer,
who'll lead the world into shadow.

23
00:01:29,804 --> 00:01:32,406
Yeah, thanks, Ianto,
I can do without the superstition.

24
00:01:32,507 --> 00:01:36,143
You people love any story that denies
the randomness of existence.

25
00:01:36,244 --> 00:01:37,678
Thanks. That makes me feel a lot better.

26
00:01:37,779 --> 00:01:41,748
Okay, I've been fielding calls all night,
the government, U NIT, the CIA.

27
00:01:41,849 --> 00:01:45,786
Half the Western world and a good proportion
of the Eastern are all asking the same question.

28
00:01:45,887 --> 00:01:48,088
Is this anything to do with us?

29
00:01:48,189 --> 00:01:50,424
And is it?

30
00:01:50,525 --> 00:01:53,327
I've run a profile on
every reported temporal anomaly

31
00:01:53,428 --> 00:01:55,596
and tracked any physical or temporal pattern.

32
00:01:59,701 --> 00:02:00,767
Shit.

33
00:02:00,868 --> 00:02:03,537
The cracks in time trace back here to the rift.

34
00:02:03,638 --> 00:02:07,174
This city, this H ub, is the centre.

35
00:02:07,275 --> 00:02:10,310
What you're seeing around the world
are ripples and aftershocks.

36
00:02:11,112 --> 00:02:14,815
-The rift is splintering because of you.
-What?

37
00:02:14,916 --> 00:02:17,217
You opened the rift without knowing
what you were doing.

38
00:02:17,318 --> 00:02:21,221
You've caused the temporal cracks to widen.
Time is seeping through.

39
00:02:21,322 --> 00:02:24,191
If it wasn't for me,
you two would still be in the 1940s.

40
00:02:26,594 --> 00:02:32,032
So are we gonna sit around crying into our lattes
or are we going to do something about it?

41
00:02:33,334 --> 00:02:36,970
Bring those who've fallen through time back here,
into the vaults.

42
00:02:37,071 --> 00:02:38,205
And do what with them?

43
00:02:38,306 --> 00:02:40,874
We'll deal with phase one first,
then I'll tell you about phase two.

44
00:02:40,975 --> 00:02:43,210
You can't control time, you can't send them back.

45
00:02:43,311 --> 00:02:46,613
-What are you gonna do?
-We'll think of something !

46
00:02:51,219 --> 00:02:52,519
Hey,

47
00:02:53,688 --> 00:02:56,256
this is not the end of the world.

48
00:02:59,394 --> 00:03:01,361
I'm certain of that.

49
00:03:04,899 --> 00:03:06,533
(COMPUTER BEEPING)

50
00:03:08,403 --> 00:03:12,939
Priority one attendance requested at the hospital.
Mortality rate's gone through the roof.

51
00:03:13,041 --> 00:03:15,442
They're sealing off the area
and designating a hot zone.

52
00:03:15,543 --> 00:03:16,843
-I'll go.
-Tosh, go with him.

53
00:03:16,944 --> 00:03:18,512
No, thanks, I'm fine on my own.

54
00:03:18,613 --> 00:03:22,349
And you'll be even better with me alongside.
Shut up and come on.

55
00:03:24,819 --> 00:03:26,853
Did you have to pick on him in public like that?

56
00:03:26,954 --> 00:03:28,789
All of our actions have consequences.

57
00:03:28,890 --> 00:03:32,125
And all your staff have feelings, Jack, even Owen.

58
00:03:32,226 --> 00:03:34,194
Well, you would know.

59
00:03:38,099 --> 00:03:39,433
He brought you back.

60
00:03:39,534 --> 00:03:40,767
(MOBILE RINGING)

61
00:03:40,868 --> 00:03:43,103
Would you rather be stuck in World War II?

62
00:03:43,171 --> 00:03:44,471
Hello?

63
00:03:44,572 --> 00:03:47,240
Gwen, it's Andy.

64
00:03:47,341 --> 00:03:49,876
Listen, I didn't know who else to call.

65
00:03:50,278 --> 00:03:52,079
(YELLING)

66
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:56,149
Double murder. Stabbed two blokes in Penarth.
Brutal, it was. No mercy.

67
00:03:57,285 --> 00:03:59,753
What are we supposed to do?
He doesn't speak a word of English.

68
00:03:59,854 --> 00:04:02,089
And he's dressed as a bloody Roman soldier!

69
00:04:02,190 --> 00:04:06,893
He's not dressed as a Roman soldier,
he is a Roman soldier and he's shouting in Latin.

70
00:04:06,994 --> 00:04:10,464
-Only word I could pick out was Gelligaer.
-Gelligaer?

71
00:04:11,032 --> 00:04:14,668
There's a Roman fort out in Gelligaer.
Built around 75 AD.

72
00:04:14,769 --> 00:04:18,305
So he was on his way there,
time splintered and he ends up here.

73
00:04:18,406 --> 00:04:19,906
Excuse me?

74
00:04:20,708 --> 00:04:23,610
H i, any time you feel like talking sense...

75
00:04:23,711 --> 00:04:27,614
-That soldier came through a crack in time.
-He's not serious, is he?

76
00:04:27,715 --> 00:04:30,417
This sort of thing just doesn't happen.
Not in Cardiff.

77
00:04:30,518 --> 00:04:32,753
Just because you can't understand it,
doesn't mean it isn't true.

78
00:04:32,854 --> 00:04:35,355
I know it sounds mad, Andy, but...

79
00:04:35,456 --> 00:04:40,827
All right, Mulder and Scully, say I do believe you,
which I don't, 'cause it's bollocks,

80
00:04:40,928 --> 00:04:45,031
but say I do, how exactly are we meant to
handle a prisoner from 2,000 years ago?

81
00:04:45,133 --> 00:04:49,202
Has he got the same rights as anyone else?
How's this gonna work with the CPS?

82
00:04:49,303 --> 00:04:50,937
We'll take him off your hands.

83
00:04:51,939 --> 00:04:53,373
(YELLING)

84
00:04:59,046 --> 00:05:01,681
Under any other circumstances,
an exuberant Roman soldier

85
00:05:01,783 --> 00:05:04,117
would be my idea of a perfect morning.

86
00:05:04,318 --> 00:05:05,852
Careful, Jack.

87
00:05:14,962 --> 00:05:17,964
Everyone's saying it, you know.
In work, on the streets.

88
00:05:19,867 --> 00:05:21,401
Do you think this is the end of the world?

89
00:05:21,502 --> 00:05:25,739
Oh, Andy, don't be silly. Do you think
the world's gonna end on your shift?

90
00:05:27,008 --> 00:05:30,110
I've seen you use that smile on a lot of people.

91
00:05:30,211 --> 00:05:33,313
-What smile?
-The smile you use to reassure people

92
00:05:33,414 --> 00:05:36,650
when deep down when you know
everything's going to shit.

93
00:05:38,820 --> 00:05:40,487
This was the first one to die.

94
00:05:40,588 --> 00:05:42,889
No ID on her, she just appeared
in the middle of AandE.

95
00:05:42,990 --> 00:05:46,293
Nobody saw her come through the doors,
she didn't register at the desk.

96
00:05:46,394 --> 00:05:47,594
So what happened?

97
00:05:47,695 --> 00:05:50,664
She started coughing up blood,
we moved her into isolation immediately.

98
00:05:50,765 --> 00:05:54,801
An hour or so later, the staff
started presenting similar symptoms.

99
00:05:55,670 --> 00:05:57,103
Which were?

100
00:05:57,205 --> 00:06:02,175
Bite-like bumps on the skin, chills, fever,
headaches, along with black patches on the skin.

101
00:06:02,276 --> 00:06:05,145
Indicating bleeding into the skin
and possibly other organs.

102
00:06:05,246 --> 00:06:07,080
From the staff,
it started spreading to other patients

103
00:06:07,181 --> 00:06:09,683
who'd been in reception when she came in.

104
00:06:12,320 --> 00:06:14,054
These aren't contemporary clothes.

105
00:06:14,155 --> 00:06:17,090
Her teeth aren't exactly modern style, either.

106
00:06:20,261 --> 00:06:21,661
Shit.

107
00:06:21,762 --> 00:06:25,799
As soon as we realised the rate of infection,
we closed down the whole area.

108
00:06:27,602 --> 00:06:29,736
How many others are infected?

109
00:06:29,837 --> 00:06:32,706
-30, maybe 40.
-OWEN : All quarantined off?

110
00:06:32,807 --> 00:06:34,074
We think so.

111
00:06:34,175 --> 00:06:37,677
Have their clothes and
their sheets destroyed immediately.

112
00:06:43,584 --> 00:06:44,851
(PANTING)

113
00:06:44,952 --> 00:06:47,921
-What is it?
-That woman isn't from this century.

114
00:06:49,457 --> 00:06:51,925
More like the 14th.

115
00:06:52,026 --> 00:06:55,595
(STAMMERING) It's the fucking Black Death, Tosh.

116
00:06:57,198 --> 00:07:01,501
She's infected Cardiff AandE with the plague
and it's my fault.

117
00:07:03,671 --> 00:07:06,506
The team are instigating procedures.

118
00:07:07,642 --> 00:07:10,844
The infected will need 30 milligrams
of streptomycin and chloramphenicol

119
00:07:10,945 --> 00:07:12,612
plus two of tetracycline.

120
00:07:12,713 --> 00:07:15,715
That's plague medicine.
Standard issue for bubonic.

121
00:07:17,285 --> 00:07:19,519
Well done, House. That's what you're up against.

122
00:07:19,620 --> 00:07:21,655
So what are you gonna do now?

123
00:07:21,756 --> 00:07:23,690
Well, you're a hospital.
You've got procedures, haven't you?

124
00:07:23,791 --> 00:07:26,426
Yes, but everybody said Torchwood
would sort it out.

125
00:07:26,527 --> 00:07:28,361
What if we get more carriers appearing
out of the blue?

126
00:07:28,462 --> 00:07:30,263
We're working to stop that.

127
00:07:30,364 --> 00:07:32,132
We waited for you !

128
00:07:32,233 --> 00:07:35,001
You've got to stop this!
You've got to do something !

129
00:07:35,102 --> 00:07:37,103
No, you've got to do something.

130
00:07:37,204 --> 00:07:38,805
People are dropping through time,

131
00:07:38,906 --> 00:07:42,075
and they are gonna bring
every disease in history through your doors.

132
00:07:42,176 --> 00:07:44,477
-So you'd better be ready!
-Owen.

133
00:07:44,578 --> 00:07:48,248
You scared enough yet? 'Cause fuck knows I am !

134
00:07:48,349 --> 00:07:50,083
Come on, Tosh !

135
00:07:50,818 --> 00:07:54,387
Make sure they get the medicine.
Call us if things get worse.

136
00:07:54,488 --> 00:07:57,023
How much worse can they get?

137
00:08:03,965 --> 00:08:05,098
Owen?

138
00:08:06,634 --> 00:08:07,767
Owen !

139
00:08:09,470 --> 00:08:11,838
(WOMAN ON PA)

140
00:08:14,141 --> 00:08:15,642
(SPEAKING IN JAPAN ESE)

141
00:08:16,177 --> 00:08:18,144
(SPEAKING IN JAPAN ESE)

142
00:08:36,897 --> 00:08:39,866
Tosh. Come on, stop pissing about!

143
00:08:48,843 --> 00:08:51,411
GWEN : If Owen managed to open the rift
to get you and Tosh back,

144
00:08:51,512 --> 00:08:53,246
can't we do the same for these people?

145
00:08:53,347 --> 00:08:55,148
We've still got the Rift Manipulator.

146
00:08:55,249 --> 00:08:57,784
(SCOFFS) There's a world of difference.

147
00:08:57,885 --> 00:09:02,889
We're talking about taking control of time,
not bringing two people back from the past.

148
00:09:02,990 --> 00:09:05,658
Besides, look at the damage Owen caused.

149
00:09:05,760 --> 00:09:09,362
We mess with it further,
we'll put the whole planet in danger.

150
00:09:10,631 --> 00:09:12,065
Have I ever let you down?

151
00:09:17,038 --> 00:09:18,905
MAN : Gwen?

152
00:09:19,006 --> 00:09:20,473
Gwen?

153
00:09:29,250 --> 00:09:30,550
I'm sorry.

154
00:09:32,186 --> 00:09:33,953
I'm so sorry.

155
00:09:37,425 --> 00:09:38,658
Gwen.

156
00:09:39,860 --> 00:09:41,594
Gwen ! Come on.

157
00:09:43,631 --> 00:09:44,798
H ustle.

158
00:09:57,711 --> 00:10:00,046
JACK: Are you sure it was the same guy?

159
00:10:00,147 --> 00:10:03,483
It was definitely him.
Bilis the caretaker at the dance hall.

160
00:10:03,584 --> 00:10:06,686
That's all he said? Sorry?
What's he got to be sorry for?

161
00:10:07,421 --> 00:10:09,155
Coming through !

162
00:10:09,223 --> 00:10:10,790
(SNARLING)

163
00:10:14,161 --> 00:10:17,764
Thirteen more reports of Weevils on the loose.
We're not gonna keep up at this rate.

164
00:10:17,865 --> 00:10:20,467
-Everything's on the increase.
-Can we stop them from making that noise?

165
00:10:20,568 --> 00:10:22,969
-If you've got any ideas how.
-Maybe they're time-sensitive.

166
00:10:23,070 --> 00:10:25,205
This disturbance may be too much for them.

167
00:10:25,306 --> 00:10:27,907
We're now full in all vaults across all nine levels.

168
00:10:28,008 --> 00:10:29,742
IANTO: Do you want me to activate
the vaults below?

169
00:10:29,844 --> 00:10:32,445
It's just we've never used them
since I've been here.

170
00:10:32,513 --> 00:10:33,613
Do it.

171
00:10:33,714 --> 00:10:37,150
Gwen, maybe you're right.
Let's run a search on your dance hall buddy.

172
00:10:37,251 --> 00:10:39,219
-We need to find him.
-Okay.

173
00:10:41,155 --> 00:10:43,223
(MOANING)

174
00:10:46,927 --> 00:10:48,161
Hello, Ianto.

175
00:10:59,039 --> 00:11:01,841
What do you want? Why are you here?

176
00:11:01,942 --> 00:11:03,643
This isn't happening.

177
00:11:05,412 --> 00:11:08,648
There's only one way to stop this
before things get worse.

178
00:11:09,650 --> 00:11:13,353
People will die, Ianto, thousands of people,

179
00:11:14,622 --> 00:11:16,556
unless you open the rift.

180
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:34,841
Owen. How was the hospital?

181
00:11:34,942 --> 00:11:38,511
Laugh a bloody minute.
They've got an outbreak of the Black Death.

182
00:11:38,612 --> 00:11:40,246
What? Oh, my God.

183
00:11:41,248 --> 00:11:43,249
Have they got it under control?

184
00:11:43,984 --> 00:11:45,885
Tosh ! How are they coping?

185
00:11:45,986 --> 00:11:51,024
Owen got the place quarantined and organised
treatments for those who've been infected.

186
00:11:51,125 --> 00:11:53,660
Only consolation is it's treatable these days.

187
00:11:53,761 --> 00:11:56,729
But, you know, what happens when
the next carrier comes through, Jack?

188
00:11:56,830 --> 00:11:59,465
Someone carrying smallpox or Ebola
or something from the future

189
00:11:59,567 --> 00:12:01,201
we don't even know about yet,
what do we do then?

190
00:12:01,302 --> 00:12:03,736
Well, it's not doing us any good
standing around speculating.

191
00:12:03,837 --> 00:12:05,271
We need to be prepared.

192
00:12:05,372 --> 00:12:10,043
We're helpless, all we're doing here
is putting sticking plasters on gaping wounds!

193
00:12:10,144 --> 00:12:11,778
What do you suggest?

194
00:12:11,879 --> 00:12:15,982
I suggest you lead us and you tell us
what the instructions are.

195
00:12:16,083 --> 00:12:18,551
-Owen...
-No, come on.

196
00:12:19,486 --> 00:12:22,255
You're all thinking it, too.
You're the big man here.

197
00:12:22,356 --> 00:12:24,924
You keep all the secrets!
Well, now's the time to tell us a few

198
00:12:25,025 --> 00:12:27,927
and tell us how the hell
we're going to get out of this!

199
00:12:29,530 --> 00:12:32,632
You want to know a secret? There is no solution.

200
00:12:33,567 --> 00:12:35,268
I can't fix this.

201
00:12:35,369 --> 00:12:38,137
Because this was never meant to happen.

202
00:12:38,239 --> 00:12:42,208
The first thing you learnt when you joined
Torchwood was don't mess with the rift.

203
00:12:42,309 --> 00:12:46,446
But you disobeyed those orders and now
everything that's happening is down to you.

204
00:12:46,547 --> 00:12:48,581
I only disobeyed instructions to get you back!

205
00:12:48,682 --> 00:12:52,352
-And now people are dying.
-What, so I shouldn't have bothered?

206
00:12:52,453 --> 00:12:54,787
Who the fuck are you anyway?

207
00:12:54,888 --> 00:12:59,259
Jack Harkness? You don't even exist.
We've looked.

208
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:03,463
So if you're not even a real person,
then why the hell should I follow your orders?

209
00:13:03,564 --> 00:13:04,931
Get out.

210
00:13:05,766 --> 00:13:07,934
-What?
-Get out!

211
00:13:08,035 --> 00:13:09,702
I'm relieving you of your duty.

212
00:13:09,803 --> 00:13:12,105
-No. You can't do that!
-Bollocks you are!

213
00:13:12,206 --> 00:13:13,439
Jack, wait.

214
00:13:15,409 --> 00:13:17,110
You're done here.

215
00:13:18,946 --> 00:13:20,146
What, so that's it?

216
00:13:20,247 --> 00:13:23,216
The whole world is going to shit
and you're gonna fire me?

217
00:13:23,317 --> 00:13:27,553
For God's sake! Both of you !
We need to stick together on this.

218
00:13:29,723 --> 00:13:34,761
If I can't rely on you, if I don't have
your complete trust, you don't belong here.

219
00:13:36,330 --> 00:13:38,197
That goes for the rest of you.

220
00:13:38,799 --> 00:13:41,668
Anyone who agrees with Owen, leave now!

221
00:13:54,882 --> 00:13:56,883
So now we know how it is.

222
00:13:59,753 --> 00:14:03,256
So that leaves me 24 hours
to savour the good times.

223
00:14:03,357 --> 00:14:05,692
What are you talking about?

224
00:14:05,793 --> 00:14:07,727
Think about it, Gwen.

225
00:14:08,395 --> 00:14:10,396
Nobody leaves this place intact.

226
00:14:11,265 --> 00:14:13,766
Some time in the next 24 hours,

227
00:14:15,135 --> 00:14:16,836
I get retconned.

228
00:14:17,771 --> 00:14:19,772
All my memories erased.

229
00:14:22,242 --> 00:14:25,445
I don't know where or when, but he'll get me.

230
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:28,314
Jack, this has gone far enough.

231
00:14:31,785 --> 00:14:33,920
Well, I guess this is goodbye.

232
00:14:37,257 --> 00:14:39,359
Good luck with the end of the world.

233
00:14:42,830 --> 00:14:45,131
I would say thanks for the memories.

234
00:14:46,033 --> 00:14:47,633
Jack, for God's sake!

235
00:15:29,443 --> 00:15:33,012
IANTO: Okay, guys, Bilis' shop is coming up
20 metres on your left.

236
00:15:42,656 --> 00:15:43,790
Wow.

237
00:15:45,359 --> 00:15:47,960
Some of this stuff must go back centuries.

238
00:15:49,630 --> 00:15:53,933
He scavenges antique pieces from the past,
brings them here, sells them for a profit.

239
00:15:54,034 --> 00:15:56,068
Not a bad business plan.

240
00:15:56,170 --> 00:15:58,438
We all have to earn a living.

241
00:15:59,540 --> 00:16:03,810
-JACK: You're from 1941.
-As you were. Hello, again.

242
00:16:08,248 --> 00:16:11,184
How can you be in two time zones at once?

243
00:16:11,285 --> 00:16:16,155
I can step across eras,
like you'd walk into another room.

244
00:16:16,256 --> 00:16:20,593
At first, it was the most incredible gift.
Now I know the reality.

245
00:16:21,528 --> 00:16:22,962
It's a curse.

246
00:16:23,797 --> 00:16:24,997
Why?

247
00:16:26,533 --> 00:16:29,669
I can see the whole of history,

248
00:16:30,537 --> 00:16:33,139
but I don't belong anywhere within it.

249
00:16:36,243 --> 00:16:40,146
So, your return to this time had a price.

250
00:16:40,247 --> 00:16:42,548
Time's splintering.

251
00:16:42,649 --> 00:16:45,751
This city exists on a rift in time.

252
00:16:46,420 --> 00:16:49,889
The only way to make it right
is to fully open that rift.

253
00:16:49,990 --> 00:16:52,492
Let it suck back what fell through.

254
00:16:53,160 --> 00:16:56,996
-No way. It's too dangerous.
-Can we even do that?

255
00:16:57,097 --> 00:17:00,566
Of course you can. Isn't that right, Captain?

256
00:17:04,271 --> 00:17:06,939
-Jack?
-You've seen what happened.

257
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:09,876
If we open that rift fully,
millions of lives will be at risk.

258
00:17:09,977 --> 00:17:13,412
And yet if you don't, more will fall through.

259
00:17:13,514 --> 00:17:16,482
Lives will be lost.

260
00:17:17,251 --> 00:17:18,918
(LAUGHING)

261
00:17:22,890 --> 00:17:26,192
-You know so much, you're coming back with us.
-I'm sorry.

262
00:17:29,596 --> 00:17:30,863
Damn it!

263
00:17:30,964 --> 00:17:33,699
Trace the temporal activity round this location.

264
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:36,569
We need to find out where he is. Come on.

265
00:17:41,041 --> 00:17:43,409
(WHISPERING) Gwen.

266
00:17:50,484 --> 00:17:52,685
I am not your enemy.

267
00:17:53,820 --> 00:17:56,889
In the cells, why did you say you were sorry?

268
00:17:56,990 --> 00:17:59,792
Sometimes it's better to live in ignorance,

269
00:18:01,261 --> 00:18:02,361
unless...

270
00:18:04,698 --> 00:18:07,233
Do you really want to know?

271
00:18:07,334 --> 00:18:08,834
Know what?

272
00:18:08,936 --> 00:18:11,003
Hold my hands. I'll show you.

273
00:18:12,072 --> 00:18:15,741
-Okay.
-Only if you're sure.

274
00:18:17,044 --> 00:18:18,578
I'm sure.

275
00:18:22,382 --> 00:18:23,649
(GASPING)

276
00:18:35,295 --> 00:18:36,562
I'm sorry.

277
00:18:37,731 --> 00:18:40,800
-What did you just show me?
-The future.

278
00:18:47,808 --> 00:18:49,442
What took you so long?

279
00:18:50,677 --> 00:18:51,877
Gwen?

280
00:18:53,013 --> 00:18:54,180
Gwen !

281
00:19:03,490 --> 00:19:05,157
Is that you?

282
00:19:06,460 --> 00:19:07,593
Yeah.

283
00:19:08,695 --> 00:19:09,996
It's me.

284
00:19:10,564 --> 00:19:11,897
(LAUGHS)

285
00:19:11,999 --> 00:19:14,533
-You're cleaning the oven !
-Aye, somebody got to, love.

286
00:19:14,635 --> 00:19:15,801
We got to go.

287
00:19:15,902 --> 00:19:17,837
-Why, what's happened?
-We've got to go, that's all.

288
00:19:17,938 --> 00:19:20,640
-Let me finish here first.
-Rhys, we've got to go now!

289
00:19:20,741 --> 00:19:23,242
Oh, here we go again, look,
always a hurry with you,

290
00:19:23,343 --> 00:19:25,811
ever since you started that bloody job...

291
00:19:28,081 --> 00:19:29,315
I'm sorry.

292
00:19:36,556 --> 00:19:38,724
(TECH NO MUSIC PLAYING)

293
00:19:42,929 --> 00:19:44,530
WOMAN : Owen.

294
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:47,700
Owen.

295
00:19:48,802 --> 00:19:50,569
(GASPS) No!

296
00:19:51,505 --> 00:19:53,673
Jesus. Diane.

297
00:19:56,877 --> 00:19:59,245
-Oh, Jesus.
-I'm lost, Owen.

298
00:20:04,051 --> 00:20:07,219
I can touch you. I don't understand.

299
00:20:07,854 --> 00:20:12,324
-Where did you end up?
-Please, bring me back, Owen.

300
00:20:12,426 --> 00:20:15,594
-You can do that, can't you?
-I don't know.

301
00:20:17,464 --> 00:20:20,166
-Everything's out of sync.
-Please.

302
00:20:21,101 --> 00:20:24,804
Please, bring me back. Open the rift.

303
00:20:27,474 --> 00:20:29,842
Do you want another drink there, mate?

304
00:20:53,433 --> 00:20:57,169
Whoa, whoa, take it easy.

305
00:20:57,270 --> 00:20:59,705
What's going on?

306
00:20:59,806 --> 00:21:01,907
Am I dreaming?

307
00:21:02,008 --> 00:21:03,642
This is where I work.

308
00:21:04,745 --> 00:21:07,346
-You work in a prison?
-These are just the cells.

309
00:21:10,016 --> 00:21:12,952
You locked me in a cell?
What the hell are you playing at?

310
00:21:13,053 --> 00:21:14,487
I was just trying to keep you safe.

311
00:21:14,588 --> 00:21:17,356
-I was safe at home!
-No, you weren't.

312
00:21:17,457 --> 00:21:18,758
You really weren't.

313
00:21:18,859 --> 00:21:22,361
Listen here, Gwen,
you better tell me exactly what's going on.

314
00:21:22,462 --> 00:21:25,164
'Cause I've taken some shit
over the past few months.

315
00:21:25,265 --> 00:21:29,835
-I mean, what's all this?
-Rhys, listen to me, I need you to trust me.

316
00:21:29,936 --> 00:21:33,005
Okay, it may not seem like it at the moment,

317
00:21:34,274 --> 00:21:37,109
but I am just trying to take care of you.

318
00:21:38,178 --> 00:21:39,845
I love you, sweetheart.

319
00:21:40,714 --> 00:21:42,114
(MU FFLED GROANING)

320
00:21:42,215 --> 00:21:43,682
What the hell was that?

321
00:21:43,784 --> 00:21:47,453
Just try and relax and I'll come back for you.

322
00:21:47,954 --> 00:21:50,422
What do you mean?
Hey, you're not going to leave me down here!

323
00:21:50,524 --> 00:21:52,424
-I'm sorry.
-Gwen !

324
00:21:52,492 --> 00:21:53,726
Gwen !

325
00:21:54,327 --> 00:21:56,662
-I'm sorry.
-Shit!

326
00:22:06,173 --> 00:22:09,441
-Did he wake up?
-Yeah. Yeah, he did.

327
00:22:10,110 --> 00:22:12,411
Tosh, can you bring up the CCTV of the vaults?

328
00:22:12,512 --> 00:22:15,247
Just leave it on the screen,
I know it sounds crazy but...

329
00:22:15,749 --> 00:22:17,049
Sure, no problem.

330
00:22:17,150 --> 00:22:20,553
Thank you, for helping me bring him here.

331
00:22:21,888 --> 00:22:24,857
I can't understand how
Bilis was able to show you that vision.

332
00:22:29,262 --> 00:22:32,531
It was so real, Tosh. I was in my flat.

333
00:22:33,466 --> 00:22:37,903
It smelt like my flat,
it had all the sounds of my flat.

334
00:22:38,004 --> 00:22:41,740
I touched the blood.
I can still feel it on my hands. Rhys' blood.

335
00:22:44,611 --> 00:22:46,779
It's not gonna happen.

336
00:22:52,953 --> 00:22:55,454
Come on, there's still work to be done.

337
00:23:00,994 --> 00:23:04,129
IANTO: What's going on?
TOSHIKO: We've got a security breach.

338
00:23:04,231 --> 00:23:05,998
(ALARM BLARING)

339
00:23:06,099 --> 00:23:09,068
All right, nobody panic.

340
00:23:09,502 --> 00:23:10,703
Rhys!

341
00:23:41,434 --> 00:23:43,669
Oh, do you work here?

342
00:23:47,173 --> 00:23:51,343
I'm Rhys, Gwen's boyfriend.

343
00:24:44,464 --> 00:24:47,433
No! Rhys, please, please, God !

344
00:24:47,500 --> 00:24:48,901
Please, God !

345
00:24:49,502 --> 00:24:50,703
No!

346
00:24:55,308 --> 00:24:57,943
We can bring... We can bring him back!

347
00:24:58,445 --> 00:25:01,180
-There's nothing we can do.
-Yes, there is!

348
00:25:02,015 --> 00:25:06,051
My boy, what am I gonna do?
What am I going to do?

349
00:25:06,486 --> 00:25:07,886
(SCREAMING)

350
00:25:11,091 --> 00:25:12,257
No!

351
00:25:39,753 --> 00:25:41,687
I'll have to tell his family.

352
00:25:43,256 --> 00:25:44,957
IANTO: We'll deal with it.

353
00:25:45,058 --> 00:25:47,993
The way you dealt with that porter
first time I met you.

354
00:25:49,896 --> 00:25:54,466
No, you won't deal with him, Ianto.

355
00:25:57,604 --> 00:26:00,472
Gwen, I'm so sorry.

356
00:26:08,681 --> 00:26:10,282
You never even met him.

357
00:26:14,654 --> 00:26:16,422
This is what happens here.

358
00:26:19,492 --> 00:26:21,193
We all end up alone.

359
00:26:26,032 --> 00:26:27,566
Not me.

360
00:26:29,536 --> 00:26:31,203
No way.

361
00:26:31,304 --> 00:26:33,172
You bring him back.

362
00:26:33,740 --> 00:26:35,841
-No.
-The resurrection gauntlet...

363
00:26:35,942 --> 00:26:37,109
Was destroyed.

364
00:26:37,210 --> 00:26:38,944
-We've got to have something else.
-I said no.

365
00:26:39,045 --> 00:26:43,048
No, there's something wrong with time
so we can go back

366
00:26:43,149 --> 00:26:45,117
-to the moment, to the very moment...
-Gwen.

367
00:26:45,218 --> 00:26:50,989
Well, there's got to be something that you can do
otherwise what's the fucking point of you?

368
00:26:51,091 --> 00:26:54,093
You, you bring him back! You bring him back!

369
00:26:54,194 --> 00:26:55,727
Bring him to me!

370
00:26:55,829 --> 00:27:00,466
You bring him back!
Do you understand me, Jack fucking Harkness?

371
00:27:01,134 --> 00:27:03,335
-Do you?
-I'm so sorry.

372
00:27:03,403 --> 00:27:05,170
I'm sorry.

373
00:27:05,271 --> 00:27:07,005
(SOBBING)

374
00:27:16,049 --> 00:27:17,349
Oh, shit.

375
00:27:20,987 --> 00:27:23,956
-What happened?
-You came back!

376
00:27:24,057 --> 00:27:26,024
Are you all right? You okay? Are you all right?

377
00:27:26,126 --> 00:27:27,926
Don't touch me!

378
00:27:36,703 --> 00:27:39,104
How many other people have got to suffer?

379
00:27:45,512 --> 00:27:47,212
I'm gonna fix this.

380
00:27:48,748 --> 00:27:50,482
I'm opening the rift.

381
00:27:54,320 --> 00:27:56,288
Make sure you stop him.

382
00:27:59,225 --> 00:28:00,425
No.

383
00:28:03,496 --> 00:28:05,297
We're gonna help him.

384
00:28:07,934 --> 00:28:13,005
Bilis was right. He said, "Open the rift
and everything goes back to normal."

385
00:28:13,106 --> 00:28:16,308
Owen's right. I'm going to get Rhys back.

386
00:28:17,043 --> 00:28:18,577
-Gwen.
-No!

387
00:28:18,645 --> 00:28:19,811
Gwen !

388
00:28:19,913 --> 00:28:21,813
Enter Emergency Protocol One.

389
00:28:23,016 --> 00:28:24,950
Out of the way, I'll do this.

390
00:28:25,051 --> 00:28:26,618
(ALARM BLARING)

391
00:28:33,226 --> 00:28:35,661
Get away from the computer, Gwen.

392
00:28:36,963 --> 00:28:40,832
This is a trap. All these cracks
around the world, they're diversions.

393
00:28:40,934 --> 00:28:42,401
This is what Bilis wants.

394
00:28:42,502 --> 00:28:44,169
What are you afraid of, Jack?

395
00:28:46,906 --> 00:28:48,207
Rhea Silva.

396
00:28:50,410 --> 00:28:52,144
I said move.

397
00:28:54,747 --> 00:28:57,149
-What the hell are you doing?
-Final warning.

398
00:29:01,621 --> 00:29:03,622
Come on, Jack.

399
00:29:03,723 --> 00:29:06,258
You're a united front now.

400
00:29:08,628 --> 00:29:13,265
Toshiko, the poor girl who'll screw
any passing alien that gives her a pendant?

401
00:29:13,766 --> 00:29:18,971
Owen, so strong, he gets in a cage with a Weevil,
desperate to be mauled.

402
00:29:19,072 --> 00:29:22,074
Ianto, hiding his Cyber-girlfriend in the basement.

403
00:29:22,175 --> 00:29:25,143
Your three comrades here
pumped bullets into her, remember?

404
00:29:25,245 --> 00:29:27,079
I've got to get Rhys back.

405
00:29:28,381 --> 00:29:33,418
Yeah, 'cause you're so in love with Rhys
that you spent half your time in Owen's bed.

406
00:29:34,454 --> 00:29:36,088
Fuck you !

407
00:29:36,189 --> 00:29:37,990
We're relieving you of your command, Captain !

408
00:29:38,091 --> 00:29:41,260
We're opening that rift
and getting back what we lost!

409
00:29:47,533 --> 00:29:49,701
-Shit!
-OWEN : Stay down !

410
00:29:51,104 --> 00:29:55,307
You wanna be in charge, Owen?
You got to have significantly bigger balls.

411
00:30:07,420 --> 00:30:09,488
I'm sick of people doubting me.

412
00:30:12,425 --> 00:30:14,660
What have you done?

413
00:30:35,381 --> 00:30:37,049
We've still got to do Jack's.

414
00:31:05,144 --> 00:31:07,312
(ALARM BLARING)

415
00:31:09,882 --> 00:31:11,216
(GROWLS)

416
00:31:12,018 --> 00:31:13,285
(SCREAMING)

417
00:31:20,693 --> 00:31:21,960
(GASPING)

418
00:31:22,095 --> 00:31:23,195
Oh, my God.

419
00:31:24,364 --> 00:31:26,131
What have you done?

420
00:31:47,420 --> 00:31:49,287
Help me move him !

421
00:31:51,357 --> 00:31:53,291
GWEN : Quick!

422
00:32:06,339 --> 00:32:07,406
Go!

423
00:32:21,754 --> 00:32:24,222
-OWEN : Keep moving.
-Right, Jack...

424
00:32:24,323 --> 00:32:26,558
everything is going to go back to normal.

425
00:32:35,902 --> 00:32:39,771
From out of the darkness, he is come.

426
00:32:40,673 --> 00:32:42,541
What is he talking about?

427
00:32:42,642 --> 00:32:45,811
Son of the Great Beast,

428
00:32:45,912 --> 00:32:49,314
cast out before time, chained in rock

429
00:32:49,415 --> 00:32:52,651
and imprisoned beneath the rift.

430
00:32:52,718 --> 00:32:54,453
What?

431
00:32:56,456 --> 00:33:02,160
All hail, Abaddon, the Great Devourer.

432
00:33:03,262 --> 00:33:05,697
Come to feast on life.

433
00:33:05,765 --> 00:33:07,399
(ROARING)

434
00:33:13,339 --> 00:33:18,043
The whole world shall die beneath his shadow.

435
00:33:31,791 --> 00:33:33,892
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

436
00:33:56,015 --> 00:34:00,719
I look upon you, my God,
and know my work is done.

437
00:34:16,002 --> 00:34:18,737
How do we stop it? Tell me what to do, Jack.

438
00:34:22,408 --> 00:34:25,877
Just you, get me to an open space.

439
00:34:39,492 --> 00:34:41,426
What are you gonna do?

440
00:34:41,527 --> 00:34:45,430
If Abaddon is the bringer of death,
let's see how he does with me.

441
00:34:45,531 --> 00:34:48,433
If he feeds on life,
then I'm an all-you-can-eat buffet.

442
00:34:48,534 --> 00:34:50,402
No, wait! Wait, you're too weak!

443
00:34:53,472 --> 00:34:57,008
Get out of here, go!

444
00:34:59,645 --> 00:35:01,479
Drive as fast as you can.

445
00:35:01,581 --> 00:35:03,114
Jack.

446
00:35:03,215 --> 00:35:04,683
Bring it on !

447
00:35:09,422 --> 00:35:10,855
(ROARING)

448
00:35:22,234 --> 00:35:23,802
(SCREAMING)

449
00:36:32,171 --> 00:36:33,805
(SOBBING)

450
00:36:47,653 --> 00:36:50,121
-You're here!
-Weren't you just here a minute ago?

451
00:36:50,189 --> 00:36:52,123
You're here.

452
00:36:57,763 --> 00:37:02,967
Go to bed. Get some sleep and I'll be back for you.

453
00:37:18,718 --> 00:37:20,285
You're certain?

454
00:37:22,788 --> 00:37:24,122
He's ice cold.

455
00:37:25,291 --> 00:37:26,691
No vital signs.

456
00:37:28,561 --> 00:37:30,395
GWEN : He survived when you shot him.

457
00:37:33,399 --> 00:37:35,967
When I first joined he said he couldn't die.

458
00:37:37,169 --> 00:37:38,570
He was wrong.

459
00:37:39,572 --> 00:37:40,872
I want to sit with him.

460
00:37:41,874 --> 00:37:44,275
-Gwen...
-I want to sit with him.

461
00:38:20,913 --> 00:38:22,113
Wake up.

462
00:38:42,568 --> 00:38:43,768
Jack.

463
00:38:48,641 --> 00:38:50,675
How long is she gonna do this?

464
00:39:32,852 --> 00:39:34,352
It's been days.

465
00:39:38,157 --> 00:39:40,158
We have to face up to it.

466
00:39:40,960 --> 00:39:42,560
He's not coming back.

467
00:39:43,696 --> 00:39:45,396
I believe in him.

468
00:39:47,199 --> 00:39:49,200
Let him go, Gwen.

469
00:40:34,446 --> 00:40:36,247
JACK: Thank you.

470
00:40:48,360 --> 00:40:49,961
(CH UCKLES)

471
00:41:39,545 --> 00:41:41,779
-I'm...
-I forgive you.

472
00:41:45,751 --> 00:41:47,485
(CRYING)

473
00:42:08,507 --> 00:42:11,209
What's happened to the rift?

474
00:42:11,310 --> 00:42:14,078
It closed up when Abaddon was destroyed.

475
00:42:14,179 --> 00:42:16,381
But it's gonna be more volatile than ever.

476
00:42:17,449 --> 00:42:22,120
The visions we had. We all saw people we loved.

477
00:42:24,790 --> 00:42:26,791
What did you see?

478
00:42:30,529 --> 00:42:31,662
Nothing.

479
00:42:35,567 --> 00:42:36,868
There was nothing.

480
00:42:40,205 --> 00:42:41,606
Jack...

481
00:42:43,208 --> 00:42:45,009
what would have tempted you?

482
00:42:45,110 --> 00:42:48,379
What visions would've convinced you
to open the rift?

483
00:42:49,915 --> 00:42:52,083
The right kind of doctor.

484
00:42:54,219 --> 00:42:55,420
Jack...

485
00:42:57,723 --> 00:42:59,857
Where are they with those coffees?

486
00:42:59,958 --> 00:43:01,459
(ELECTRONIC BEEPING)

487
00:43:25,717 --> 00:43:27,819
(WHOOSHING)

488
00:43:30,989 --> 00:43:32,123
Jack.

489
00:43:35,794 --> 00:43:36,928
Jack?

490
00:43:44,403 --> 00:43:47,238
-Did you see Jack on your way in?
-No.

491
00:43:48,440 --> 00:43:50,708
I thought we tidied up in here!

492
00:43:51,343 --> 00:43:53,344
What's the matter?

493
00:43:56,048 --> 00:43:57,949
He was just here.

494
00:44:00,552 --> 00:44:01,752
Something's taken him. Jack's gone.
